          {
            "title": "Question 2",
            "id": 76090,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the <code>=</code> sign for?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item correct=\"true\" value=\"1\">It gives a value to a variable</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"2\">It adds string values together</item><item correct=\"false\" value=\"3\">It divides a number by another number</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It gives a value to a variable.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>In <code>score = 9</code>, what does the <code>=</code> sign do?</p><selection multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It stores <code>9</code> in <code>score</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It displays <code>9</code> in the console</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">It joins <code>score</code> and <code>9</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick It stores <code>9</code> in <code>score</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
