          {
            "title": "Question 1",
            "id": 76943,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What sign do we use to check if two values are equal?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>==</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>=</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>()</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>==</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Use a sign to check whether two values are equal. Which line checks whether <code>score</code> has the value <code>10</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>score == 10</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>score = 10</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>score != 10</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>score == 10</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question 2",
            "id": 76942,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the result of using the <code>==</code> operator?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A value of either <code>True</code> or <code>False</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A value of either <code>\"True\"</code> or <code>\"False\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A numerical value</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A value of either <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Python evaluates <code>7 == 8</code>. What kind of value does that comparison produce?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A Boolean value: either <code>True</code> or <code>False</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A string value: either <code>\"True\"</code> or <code>\"False\"</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">A number value</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A Boolean value: either <code>True</code> or <code>False</code>.</p></body></html>"
